{
  "id": "maximum-xor-of-two-numbers",
  "questionId": "maximum-xor-of-two-numbers",
  "slug": "maximum-xor-of-two-numbers",
  "title": "Maximum XOR of Two Numbers in an Array",
  "difficulty": "Medium",
  "category": "Trie",
  "patterns": [
    "trie",
    "bit manipulation"
  ],
  "lists": [],
  "hints": [
    "XOR is maximized bit by bit, from the most significant bit down - at each bit position you WANT the two numbers to disagree (one 0, one 1)",
    "picture every number as a fixed-length binary string (say 32 bits); if you insert all of them into a trie bit by bit (MSB first), two numbers that share a long common bit-prefix are 'close' and two that diverge early are 'far' in XOR terms",
    "insert every number into this binary trie first",
    "then, for each number, walk the trie again trying at every level to step into the child representing the OPPOSITE bit of the current number's bit at that level - if that opposite child doesn't exist, you're forced to take the same-bit child instead",
    "the number formed by the bits you actually walked, XORed with the original number, is the best XOR achievable using that number as one side of the pair - track the maximum over all numbers"
  ],
  "commonMistakes": [
    "using a fixed bit width that's too small and truncating larger values (32 bits is safe for standard 32-bit integers)",
    "walking the trie greedily but forgetting to fall back to the same-bit child when the opposite-bit child doesn't exist",
    "starting the bit walk from the least significant bit instead of the most significant bit, which breaks the greedy argument"
  ],
  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You're given a list of non-negative integers `nums`.\n\n**Find the maximum value of `nums[i] XOR nums[j]` over all pairs of indices `i`, `j`.**\n\nSince XOR of a number with itself is 0, the maximum always comes from two\ndistinct positions in practice.\n",
    "constraints": [
      "2 <= nums.length <= 2 * 10^5",
      "0 <= nums[i] <= 2^31 - 1"
    ],
    "notes": [
      "an array where the two largest numbers do not produce the maximum XOR",
      "all elements identical (maximum XOR is 0)",
      "an array containing 0 alongside other values"
    ],
    "inputFormat": "Arguments passed into solution function",
    "outputFormat": "Return output matching method signature",
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
